{"subjectId":"python","id":"exceptions","title":"Exceptions & Context Managers","group":"Advanced Python","order":19,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">Errors are objects that propagate up the call stack until something handles them. <code>with</code> guarantees cleanup no matter how a block exits.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-shield\"></i>try / except / else / finally</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def parse(value):\n    try:\n        n = int(value)\n    except ValueError as e:\n        return f\"bad input: {e}\"\n    else:\n        return n * 2            # runs only if no exception\n    finally:\n        pass                    # always runs: close files, release locks\n\nprint(parse(\"21\"))              # 42\nprint(parse(\"x\"))               # bad input: invalid literal for int() with base 10: 'x'</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Block</th><th>Runs when</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>try</code></td><td>Always — the code that might fail</td></tr><tr><td><code>except E</code></td><td>An exception of type <code>E</code> (or a subclass) was raised</td></tr><tr><td><code>else</code></td><td>The <code>try</code> block finished <strong>without</strong> an exception</td></tr><tr><td><code>finally</code></td><td>Always, even after <code>return</code>, <code>break</code> or an unhandled error</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-flame\"></i>Raising &amp; custom exceptions</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>class InsufficientFunds(Exception):\n    def __init__(self, needed):\n        super().__init__(f\"need {needed} more\")\n        self.needed = needed\n\ndef withdraw(balance, amount):\n    if amount &gt; balance:\n        raise InsufficientFunds(amount - balance)\n    return balance - amount\n\ntry:\n    withdraw(100, 150)\nexcept InsufficientFunds as e:\n    print(e, e.needed)          # need 50 more 50\n\ntry:\n    try:\n        {}[\"k\"]\n    except KeyError as e:\n        raise LookupError(\"config missing\") from e    # keep the original cause\nexcept LookupError as e:\n    print(repr(e.__cause__))    # KeyError('k')</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"grid\"><div class=\"callout callout--good\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Do</div><p>Catch the most specific exception you can handle, keep <code>try</code> blocks small, and re-raise with <code>raise</code> (no argument) to preserve the traceback.</p></div><div class=\"callout callout--bad\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Avoid</div><p>Bare <code>except:</code> or <code>except Exception: pass</code> — it hides bugs, and a bare <code>except</code> even swallows <code>KeyboardInterrupt</code>.</p></div></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-hierarchy-3\"></i>Exception hierarchy (the useful part)</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Exception</th><th>Typical cause</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>ValueError</code></td><td>Right type, wrong value: <code>int('x')</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>TypeError</code></td><td>Wrong type: <code>'a' + 1</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>KeyError</code> / <code>IndexError</code></td><td>Missing dict key / list index out of range (both are <code>LookupError</code>s)</td></tr><tr><td><code>AttributeError</code></td><td>Object has no such attribute</td></tr><tr><td><code>ZeroDivisionError</code></td><td>Division by zero (an <code>ArithmeticError</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>FileNotFoundError</code></td><td>Missing file (an <code>OSError</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>StopIteration</code></td><td>Iterator is exhausted</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-door-exit\"></i>Context managers: <code>with</code></h3>\n<p><code>with</code> calls <code>__enter__</code> at the start and <code>__exit__</code> at the end — even if the block raises. Files, locks, DB transactions and timers all use it.</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>from contextlib import contextmanager, suppress\n\n@contextmanager\ndef tag(name):\n    print(f\"&lt;{name}&gt;\")           # setup\n    try:\n        yield name               # the with-block runs here\n    finally:\n        print(f\"&lt;/{name}&gt;\")      # teardown, always\n\nwith tag(\"b\") as t:\n    print(t.upper())\n\nwith suppress(FileNotFoundError):     # ignore one specific error\n    open(\"definitely-missing.txt\")\nprint(\"still running\")</code></pre></figure>\n<figure class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>&lt;b&gt;\nB\n&lt;/b&gt;\nstill running</code></pre></figure></section>"}